    "#HumanBody",
    "#Brain",
    "#ScienceForKids"
  ],
  "tags": [
    "brain for kids",
    "how nerves work",
    "nervous system for kids",
    "five senses for kids",
    "reflexes for kids",
    "human body for kids",
    "science for kids"
  ],
  "cast": [
    "LEO",
    "MIA"
  ],
  "loop_card": {
    "text": "Brain to body?",
    "cue": "next",
    "left": "img:Human_physiology/Servier/brain-1",
    "right": "🖐️"
  },
  "lines": [
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "Mia, how does my brain talk to the rest of my body?",
      "board": {
        "type": "title",
        "left": {
          "icon": "img:Human_physiology/Servier/brain-1",
          "label": "Brain"
        },
        "right": {
          "icon": "🖐️",
          "label": "Body"
        },
        "mid": "?"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "With super-fast messages! Today we'll meet your brain, follow its messages, and find out how your senses work.",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "⚡",
        "text": "Super-fast messages",
        "cue": "super",
        "sub": "And your senses!",
        "sub_cue": "senses"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "My senses? Like seeing and hearing?"
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "Exactly! But first, let's meet the boss.",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "img:Human_physiology/Servier/brain-1",
        "text": "Meet the boss!",
        "cue": "boss"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "Your brain lives in your head, safe inside your skull. Your skull is like a built-in helmet!",
      "chapter": "Meet your brain",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "🪖",
        "text": "Safe in your skull",
        "cue": "skull",
        "sub": "A built-in helmet",
        "sub_cue": "helmet"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "What does my brain look like?"
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "It's soft and wrinkly, a bit like a giant walnut.",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "🌰",
        "text": "Soft and wrinkly",
        "cue": "wrinkly",
        "sub": "Like a walnut",
        "sub_cue": "walnut"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "And what's it made of?"
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "Billions of tiny cells called neurons. They're also called nerve cells.",
      "punch": "neurons",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "img:Cell_types/almaCELL/Neurons",
        "text": "Neurons",
        "cue": "neurons",
        "sub": "Tiny nerve cells",
        "sub_cue": "nerve"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "What does my brain actually do?"
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "Everything! It helps you think, remember, feel, move, and even dream.",
      "board": {
        "type": "gallery",
        "title": "Your brain helps you",
        "items": [
          {
            "icon": "🤔",
            "label": "Think",
            "cue": "think"
          },
          {
            "icon": "💭",
            "label": "Remember",
            "cue": "remember"
          },
          {
            "icon": "❤️",
            "label": "Feel",
            "cue": "feel"
          },
          {
            "icon": "🏃",
            "label": "Move",
            "cue": "move"
          },
          {
            "icon": "😴",
            "label": "Dream",
            "cue": "dream"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "Even when I'm asleep?"
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "Yes! It never fully switches off. While you sleep, it helps keep your heart beating and you breathing.",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "😴",
        "text": "Never switches off",
        "cue": "switches",
        "sub": "Heart and breathing",
        "sub_cue": "heart"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "But how does my brain tell my hand to wave?",
      "chapter": "Nerve messages"
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "Through nerves! Nerves are long lines of nerve cells that reach every part of your body, like tiny wires.",
      "punch": "nerves",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "⚡",
        "text": "Nerves: tiny wires",
        "cue": "nerves",
        "sub": "To every part of you",
        "sub_cue": "every"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "Real wires? Inside me?"
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "Not metal wires! Living cells. Each nerve cell passes the message to the next one, like a relay race.",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "🏃",
        "text": "Cell to cell",
        "cue": "passes",
        "sub": "Like a relay race",
        "sub_cue": "relay"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "How do messages get all the way down to my toes?"
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "Down your back runs your spinal cord, a big bundle of nerves. It's like a highway for messages.",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "🛣️",
        "text": "The spinal cord",
        "cue": "spinal",
        "sub": "A message highway",
        "sub_cue": "highway"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "So when I want to kick a ball..."
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "Your brain sends a message down your spinal cord, out along a nerve, to your leg muscles. Kick!",
      "board": {
        "type": "body",
        "title": "Kick message",
        "show": [
          "brain",
          "muscles"
        ],
        "flow": "nerves",
        "cue": "sends",
        "labels": [
          {
            "text": "Brain",
            "at": "brain",
            "cue": "brain"
          },
          {
            "text": "Kick!",
            "at": "leg",
            "cue": "kick"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "And it all happens in a blink!"
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "Messages go both ways! Down from your brain, they tell muscles to move. Up to your brain, they tell it what you sense.",
      "board": {
        "type": "compare",
        "left": {
          "label": "Down",
          "items": [
            {
              "icon": "🏃",
              "text": "Move!",
              "cue": "move"
            }
          ]
        },
        "right": {
          "label": "Up",
          "items": [
            {
              "icon": "👀",
              "text": "Sense!",
              "cue": "sense"
            }
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "So what are my senses?",
      "chapter": "Your five senses"
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "You have five main senses: sight, hearing, smell, taste and touch. Each one sends news to your brain.",
      "board": {
        "type": "gallery",
        "title": "Five senses",
        "items": [
          {
            "icon": "👀",
            "label": "Sight",
            "cue": "sight"
          },
          {
            "icon": "👂",
            "label": "Hearing",
            "cue": "hearing"
          },
          {
            "icon": "👃",
            "label": "Smell",
            "cue": "smell"
          },
          {
            "icon": "👅",
            "label": "Taste",
            "cue": "taste"
          },
          {
            "icon": "✋",
            "label": "Touch",
            "cue": "touch"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "Let's start with seeing!"
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "Light bounces off things and goes into your eyes. Your eyes turn the light into nerve messages and send them to your brain.",
      "board": {
        "type": "journey",
        "title": "How you see",
        "traveler": "✨",
        "items": [
          {
            "icon": "💡",
            "label": "Light bounces",
            "cue": "light"
          },
          {
            "icon": "img:Human_physiology/Servier/eye",
            "label": "Into your eye",
            "cue": "eyes"
          },
          {
            "icon": "⚡",
            "label": "Nerve message",
            "cue": "nerve"
          },
          {
            "icon": "img:Human_physiology/Servier/brain-1",
            "label": "Brain: I see!",
            "cue": "brain"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "So I really see with my brain?"
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "In a way, yes! Your eyes catch the light, but your brain works out what the picture means.",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "img:Human_physiology/Servier/eye",
        "text": "Eyes catch light",
        "cue": "eyes",
        "sub": "Brain makes the picture",
        "sub_cue": "brain"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "What about hearing?"
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "Sounds are tiny wiggles in the air called vibrations. Your ears catch them and send messages to your brain.",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "img:Human_physiology/Servier/ear",
        "text": "Sounds are wiggles",
        "cue": "sounds",
        "sub": "Ears catch them",
        "sub_cue": "ears"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "And smelling?"
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "When you sniff, tiny bits from a cookie float into your nose. Special cells there tell your brain: cookies!",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "img:Human_physiology/Servier/nasal-cavity",
        "text": "Sniff, sniff!",
        "cue": "sniff",
        "sub": "Smell cells in your nose",
        "sub_cue": "nose"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "Yum! What about taste?"
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "Your tongue is covered in tiny taste buds. They can tell sweet, salty, sour and bitter.",
      "board": {
        "type": "gallery",
        "title": "Taste buds",
        "items": [
          {
            "icon": "🍭",
            "label": "Sweet",
            "cue": "sweet"
          },
          {
            "icon": "🥨",
            "label": "Salty",
            "cue": "salty"
          },
          {
            "icon": "🍋",
            "label": "Sour",
            "cue": "sour"
          },
          {
            "icon": "🥦",
            "label": "Bitter",
            "cue": "bitter"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "And the last sense is touch?"
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "Yes! Your skin is full of tiny sensors. They feel soft, rough, hot, cold, and even tickles!",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "img:Human_physiology/Servier/skin-normal",
        "text": "Skin feels it all",
        "cue": "skin",
        "sub": "Even tickles!",
        "sub_cue": "tickles"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "Tickles! My favorite sense!"
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "Sometimes your body moves before your brain even thinks. That's called a reflex.",
      "chapter": "Super-fast reflexes",
      "punch": "reflex",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "⚡",
        "text": "Move before you think",
        "cue": "moves",
        "sub": "That's a reflex!",
        "sub_cue": "reflex"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "Like what?"
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "Touch something too hot, and a message zooms to your spinal cord, which says: pull away! Your hand moves before you even feel ouch.",
      "board": {
        "type": "journey",
        "title": "Hot! Pull away!",
        "traveler": "⚡",
        "items": [
          {
            "icon": "🔥",
            "label": "Too hot!",
            "cue": "hot"
          },
          {
            "icon": "🛣️",
            "label": "Spinal cord",
            "cue": "spinal"
          },
          {
            "icon": "✋",
            "label": "Pull away!",
            "cue": "pull"
          },
          {
            "icon": "img:Human_physiology/Servier/brain-1",
            "label": "Then: ouch!",
            "cue": "ouch"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "Whoa, my body protects me all by itself!"
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "Blinking is a reflex too. If something flies at your face, your eyes blink shut to keep them safe.",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "😉",
        "text": "Blink! A reflex too",
        "cue": "blinking",
        "sub": "Keeps eyes safe",
        "sub_cue": "safe"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "How can I take care of my brain?"
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "Wear a helmet when you ride your bike, get lots of sleep, drink water, and keep learning new things!",
      "board": {
        "type": "checklist",
        "title": "Brain care",
        "icon": "🧠",
        "items": [
          {
            "icon": "🪖",
            "text": "Wear a helmet",
            "cue": "helmet",
            "ok": true
          },
          {
            "icon": "😴",
            "text": "Lots of sleep",
            "cue": "sleep",
            "ok": true
          },
          {
            "icon": "💧",
            "text": "Drink water",
            "cue": "water",
            "ok": true
          },
          {
            "icon": "📚",
            "text": "Keep learning",
            "cue": "learning",
            "ok": true
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "Quiz time! Question one: what's the big highway of nerves down your back called? Think...",
      "chapter": "Quiz time",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "❓",
        "text": "Quiz time!",
        "cue": "quiz",
        "sub": "Nerve highway?",
        "sub_cue": "highway"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "The spinal cord!",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "🛣️",
        "text": "Spinal cord!",
        "cue": "spinal"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "Yes! Question two: where do your taste buds live? Think...",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "🤔",
        "text": "Where are taste buds?",
        "cue": "taste"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "On my tongue!",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "👅",
        "text": "On your tongue!",
        "cue": "tongue"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "Right! Last one: when your hand jumps away from something hot, what's that called? Think...",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "🔥",
        "text": "Hot! What's that?",
        "cue": "hot"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "A reflex!",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "⚡",
        "text": "A reflex!",
        "cue": "reflex"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "Amazing! So: your brain is the boss, nerves carry messages both ways, and your senses send news to your brain.",
      "board": {
        "type": "summary",
        "rows": [
          {
            "icon": "img:Human_physiology/Servier/brain-1",
            "text": "Brain is the boss",
            "cue": "brain"
          },
          {
            "icon": "img:Cell_types/almaCELL/Neurons",
            "text": "Nerves carry messages",
            "cue": "nerves"
          },
          {
            "icon": "👀",
            "text": "Senses send news",
            "cue": "senses"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "My brain is the boss... of fun!",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "🎉",
        "text": "Boss of fun!",
        "cue": "boss"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "It sure is! Ask a grown-up to subscribe to The Curio Kids Club for more wonders, and share this with a friend! And next time someone asks... how does my brain talk to my body?"
    }
  ]
}